    "year": 2014,
    "subject": "History",
    "format": "single",
    "stem": "Chaitra 1 of the national calendar based on the Saka Era corresponds to which one of the following dates of the Gregorian calendar in a normal year of 365 days ?",
    "options": [
      "22nd March (or 21st March)",
      "15th May (or 16th May)",
      "21st March (or 30th March)",
      "21st April (or 20th April)"
    ],
    "key": "A",
    "explanation": "India's national calendar is based on the Saka Era (starting year: 78 AD). Chaitra is the first month. Chaitra 1 falls on: 22nd March in a normal year (365 days), 21st March in a leap year (366 days). This is easy to remember: India's financial year also starts close to this date (1st April). The Saka calendar was adopted in 1957 along with the Gregorian calendar for official purposes.\r\n\r\n(Ref: India Year Book)"
