    "year": 2014,
    "subject": "Environment",
    "format": "statements",
    "stem": "With reference to 'Eco-Sensitive Zones', which of the following statements is/are correct ?\n\n1. Eco-Sensitive Zones are the areas that are declared under the Wildlife (Protection) Act,\n1972.\n2. The purpose of the declaration of Eco-Sensitive Zones is to prohibit all kinds of human activities in those zones except agriculture\n\nSelect the correct answer using the code given below.",
    "options": [
      "1 only",
      "2 only",
      "Both 1 and 2",
      "Neither 1 nor 2"
    ],
    "key": "D",
    "explanation": "Both statements are wrong.\r\n\r\n**Statement 1** — WRONG: Eco-Sensitive Zones (ESZs) are declared under the Environment (Protection) Act, 1986 — NOT the Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972. They are buffer zones around National Parks and Wildlife Sanctuaries.\r\n\r\n**Statement 2** — WRONG: ESZs do NOT prohibit ALL human activities. They regulate certain activities (like mining, large industries, major construction) but allow many others (like agriculture, rain-water harvesting, organic farming). The specific prohibitions/regulations vary from zone to zone and are notified individually by MoEF. Think of ESZs as 'transition zones' — not no-go zones."
