    "explanation": "Rivers flowing through Arunachal Pradesh: Lohit — CORRECT: Flows through eastern Arunachal Pradesh; one of the major tributaries of the Brahmaputra. It enters India at Kibithu. Subansiri — CORRECT: The largest tributary of Brahmaputra, flows through central Arunachal Pradesh. The controversial Subansiri Lower Hydroelectric Project is located at the Arunachal-Assam border. Barak — WRONG: The Barak River flows through Manipur and southern Assam (Barak Valley), NOT through Arunachal Pradesh. It eventually flows into Bangladesh and becomes the Surma and Kushiyara rivers. Memory: Arunachal's major rivers (west to east) = Kameng, Subansiri, Siang (main Brahmaputra), Dibang, Lohit. Barak is a separate river system altogether."
