    "year": 2014,
    "subject": "Environment",
    "format": "statements",
    "stem": "Consider the following international agreements :\n\n1. The international Treaty on Plant Genetic Resources for Food and Agriculture\n2. The United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification\n3. The World Heritage Convention\n\nWhich of the above has/have a bearing on the biodiversity ?",
    "options": [
      "1 and 2 only",
      "3 only",
      "1 and 3 only",
      "1, 2 and 3"
    ],
    "key": "D",
    "explanation": "All three international agreements have a bearing on biodiversity:\r\n\r\n(1) International Treaty on Plant Genetic Resources for Food and Agriculture (ITPGRFA) — DIRECTLY about biodiversity; it deals with conservation and sustainable use of plant genetic resources (crop diversity, seed banks).\r\n\r\n(2) UN Convention to Combat Desertification (UNCCD) — land degradation and desertification destroy habitats, so combating it protects biodiversity. UNCCD itself states it 'collaborates closely with the Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD).'\r\n\r\n(3) World Heritage Convention — protects natural World Heritage Sites (like Sundarbans, Western Ghats, Kaziranga), which are biodiversity hotspots. Think broadly: biodiversity is affected by agriculture, land degradation, AND habitat protection — all three conventions address one of these."
