    "year": 2016,
    "subject": "Economy",
    "format": "single",
    "stem": "Recently, which of the following States has explored the possibility of constructing an artificial inland port to be connected to sea by a long navigational channel?",
    "options": [
      "Andhra Pradesh",
      "Chhattisgarh",
      "Karnataka",
      "Rajasthan"
    ],
    "key": "D",
    "explanation": "**Answer: (d) Rajasthan**\r\n\r\nSurprisingly, landlocked Rajasthan explored building an artificial inland port! The Government of Rajasthan planned to develop an Inland Shipping Port at Jalore district, connected to the Arabian Sea by a navigational channel along the Kutch Creek in Gujarat.\r\n\r\nWhy this is tricky: Most students wouldn't associate Rajasthan (a desert state) with ports and sea connectivity. But Rajasthan's southern border is not far from Gujarat's coast.\r\n\r\n**Why not the others?**\r\n(a) Andhra Pradesh - Already has a long coastline.\r\n(b) Chhattisgarh - No such proposal.\r\n(c) Karnataka - Already has a coastline.\r\n\r\nThis was a difficult, factual current affairs question from a PIB press release."
