    "year": 2016,
    "subject": "Environment",
    "format": "statements",
    "stem": "What is/are the importance/ importances of the ‘United Convention to Combat Desertification’?\n\n1. It aims to promote effective action through innovative national programmes and supportive international partnerships\n2. It has a special/particular focus on South Asia and North Africa regions, and its Secretariat facilitates the allocation of major portion of financial resources to these regions.\n3. It is committed to bottom-up approach, encouraging the participation of local people in combating the desertification.\n\nSelect the correct answer using the code given below.",
    "options": [
      "1 only",
      "2 and 3 only",
      "1 and 3 only",
      "1, 2 and 3"
    ],
    "key": "C",
    "explanation": "**Answer: (c) 1 and 3 only**\r\n\r\n**Statement 1 (✓ CORRECT)**: UNCCD promotes effective action through innovative national programmes and supportive international partnerships. Established after the 1992 Rio Earth Summit, it is the sole legally binding agreement linking environment and development to sustainable land management.\r\n\r\n**Statement 2 (✗ WRONG)**: UNCCD does NOT have a special focus on South Asia and North Africa with major funding allocation to these regions. It addresses ALL arid, semi-arid, and dry sub-humid areas globally.\r\n\r\n**Statement 3 (✓ CORRECT)**: UNCCD is committed to bottom-up approach, encouraging local people's participation in combating desertification.\r\n\r\n**Key UNCCD facts: Established 1994; 197 parties; focuses on drylands globally; India is a signatory; Secretariat in Bonn, Germany.**"
