    "year": 2016,
    "subject": "Geography",
    "format": "single",
    "stem": "Recently, linking of which of the following rivers was undertaken?",
    "options": [
      "Cauvery and Tungabhadra",
      "Godavari and Krishna",
      "Mahanadi and Son",
      "Narmada and Tapti"
    ],
    "key": "B",
    "explanation": "**Answer: (b) Godavari and Krishna**\r\n\r\nThe Godavari-Krishna river linking was in news because of the Pattiseema Lift Irrigation Scheme in Andhra Pradesh.\r\n\r\n**Key facts: The AP government under CM Chandrababu Naidu initiated a project to divert surplus Godavari water to the Krishna river basin through the Pattiseema Lift Irrigation Scheme. It started on September 16, 2015 and was India's first major river-linking project to be completed.**\r\n\r\n**Why not the others?**\r\n(a) Cauvery and Tungabhadra - No such linking was undertaken recently.\r\n(c) Mahanadi and Son - No such recent project.\r\n(d) Narmada and Tapti - No such recent linking.\r\n\r\nThe broader context: India has a long-term National River Linking Project. The Godavari-Krishna link was one of the first to actually be implemented on the ground."
