    "subject": "Geography",
    "format": "statements",
    "stem": "Which of the following is/are tributary/ tributaries of Brahmaputra?\n\n1. Dibang\n2. Kameng\n3. Lohit\n\nSelect the correct answer using the code given below.",
    "options": [
      "1 only",
      "2 and 3 only",
      "1 and 3 only",
      "1, 2 and 3"
    ],
    "key": "D",
    "explanation": "**Answer: (d) 1, 2 and 3**\r\n\r\nAll three - Dibang, Kameng, and Lohit - are tributaries of the Brahmaputra river in northeastern India.\r\n\r\n1. Dibang - Joins Brahmaputra in Arunachal Pradesh, originates near Keya Pass.\r\n2. Kameng (called Jia Bharali in Assam) - Originates in Tawang district, Arunachal Pradesh.\r\n3. Lohit - Joins near Sadiya in Assam, originates in eastern Tibet.\r\n\r\nOther Brahmaputra tributaries: North bank - Subansiri (largest), Manas, Sankosh. South bank - Dibang, Lohit, Dhansiri, Kopili.\r\n\r\nBrahmaputra's different names: Tsangpo (Tibet), Siang/Dihang (Arunachal), Brahmaputra (Assam), Jamuna (Bangladesh).\r\n\r\nSource: NCERT Class XI, 'India: Physical Environment.'"
